# Rijkshuisstijl Design Guidelines

This project follows the **Rijkshuisstijl** (Dutch Government) design system, based on the NL Design System architecture. These guidelines ensure consistency with Dutch government design standards for accessibility, clarity, and professionalism.

## Design Philosophy

The Rijkshuisstijl emphasizes:
- **Clarity**: Clean, unambiguous interfaces
- **Accessibility**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance minimum
- **Consistency**: Predictable patterns across all interfaces
- **Professionalism**: Government-grade design quality

## Color Palette

### Primary Colors

**Primary Blue (Rijksblauw)**
- HSL: `hsl(203 100% 35%)` - Primary action color
- Hex equivalent: `#0064B0`
- Used for: Primary buttons, links, focus states, important actions

**Primary Foreground**
- HSL: `hsl(0 0% 100%)` - White text on primary backgrounds
- Ensures proper contrast on primary blue

### Secondary Colors

**Secondary**
- HSL: `hsl(210 20% 95%)` - Light gray for secondary actions
- Used for: Secondary buttons, subtle backgrounds

**Muted**
- HSL: `hsl(210 15% 96%)` - Very light gray
- Used for: Disabled states, subtle backgrounds, borders

**Muted Foreground**
- HSL: `hsl(220 10% 45%)` - Medium gray text
- Used for: Placeholder text, secondary text, hints

### Semantic Colors

**Destructive**
- HSL: `hsl(0 84% 50%)` - Red for destructive actions
- Used for: Delete buttons, error states, warnings

**Border/Input**
- HSL: `hsl(220 15% 85%)` - Light gray borders
- Used for: Input borders, card borders, dividers

### Dark Mode

Dark mode colors follow the same principles but with inverted backgrounds:
- Background: `hsl(220 30% 8%)` - Very dark blue-gray
- Foreground: `hsl(210 20% 95%)` - Light text
- Primary: `hsl(203 100% 50%)` - Brighter blue for visibility

## Typography

### Font Family

Use system fonts for optimal performance and consistency:
```css
font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
```

### Font Weights

- **Semibold (600)**: Headings, labels, important text
- **Medium (500)**: Buttons, emphasis
- **Regular (400)**: Body text, descriptions

### Line Heights

- **Headings**: `1.3` - Tighter for visual hierarchy
- **Body**: `1.5` - Comfortable reading experience
- **Labels**: `1.2` - Compact but readable

## Component Guidelines

### Buttons

**Sizing**
- Default: `h-10` (40px) - Standard clickable height
- Small: `h-8` (32px) - Compact actions
- Large: `h-12` (48px) - Primary actions, important CTAs

**States**
- Default: Primary blue background with white text
- Hover: Slightly darker (`/90` opacity)
- Active: Even darker (`/95` opacity) for tactile feedback
- Disabled: `opacity-50` with `pointer-events-none`

**Focus States**
- Ring: `ring-2` with `ring-ring` color
- Offset: `ring-offset-2` for clear visibility
- Essential for keyboard navigation accessibility

**Example**
```tsx
<Button 
  variant="default" 
  size="default"
  className="w-full"
>
  Sign In
</Button>
```

### Input Fields

**Sizing**
- Height: `h-11` (44px) - Comfortable touch target
- Padding: `px-4 py-2` - Generous padding for readability

**Borders**
- Border width: `border-2` - Clear, visible boundaries
- Border color: Uses `border-input` token

**Focus States**
- Ring: `ring-2` with `ring-ring` (primary blue)
- Offset: `ring-offset-2` for clear focus indication
- Outline: `outline-none` to remove default browser outline

**Disabled States**
- Background: `bg-muted` - Visual indication of disabled state
- Cursor: `cursor-not-allowed`
- Opacity: `opacity-50`

**Example**
```tsx
<Input
  type="email"
  placeholder="name@example.com"
  className="h-11"
  aria-describedby="email-error"
  aria-invalid={hasError}
/>
```

### Labels

**Styling**
- Font weight: `font-semibold` - Clear hierarchy
- Font size: `text-sm` - Compact but readable
- Line height: `leading-tight` - Minimal vertical space

**Accessibility**
- Always use `htmlFor` to associate with inputs
- Include ARIA attributes when needed

**Example**
```tsx
<Label htmlFor="email" className="text-base font-medium">
  Email
</Label>
```

### Forms

**Spacing**
- Field spacing: `space-y-6` - Clear separation between fields
- Label-input spacing: `space-y-2` - Tight coupling

**Error Handling**
- Error container: Uses `bg-destructive/10` with `border-destructive/20`
- Text color: `text-destructive`
- Include `role="alert"` and `id` for ARIA linking
- Link errors to inputs with `aria-describedby`

**Example**
```tsx
{error && (
  <div
    id="error-message"
    role="alert"
    className="p-4 rounded-md bg-destructive/10 border border-destructive/20 text-destructive text-sm"
  >
    {error}
  </div>
)}
```

### Cards

**Borders**
- Border width: `border-2` - Clear definition
- Shadow: `shadow-lg` - Subtle elevation

**Spacing**
- Header padding: `p-6` with `pb-6` - Generous spacing
- Content padding: `p-6 pt-0` - Connected to header

**Example**
```tsx
<Card className="w-full border-2 shadow-lg">
  <CardHeader className="pb-6">
    <CardTitle>Title</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    {/* Content */}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

## Layout Guidelines

### Auth Pages

**Background**
- Use clean white background: `bg-white`
- Avoid gradients - keep it simple and professional

**Centering**
- Use flexbox: `flex items-center justify-center`
- Container: `max-w-md` for optimal form width
- Padding: `p-4` for mobile spacing

**Example**
```tsx
<div className="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center bg-white p-4">
  <div className="w-full max-w-md">
    {/* Content */}
  </div>
</div>
```

## Accessibility Requirements

### WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance

**Color Contrast**
- Text on primary: Minimum 4.5:1 ratio
- Large text (18px+): Minimum 3:1 ratio
- Interactive elements: Clear contrast in all states

**Keyboard Navigation**
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
- Focus indicators must be clearly visible
- Logical tab order throughout the interface

**Screen Readers**
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include ARIA labels and descriptions
- Associate labels with inputs using `htmlFor`
- Use `role="alert"` for error messages
- Use `aria-invalid` for form validation states
- Use `aria-busy` for loading states

**Touch Targets**
- Minimum 44x44px (11 Tailwind units) for mobile
- Adequate spacing between clickable elements

## Best Practices

### Do's

✅ Use semantic HTML elements (`<form>`, `<button>`, `<input>`, etc.)
✅ Include proper ARIA attributes for accessibility
✅ Maintain consistent spacing using Tailwind's spacing scale
✅ Use design tokens from `index.css` for colors
✅ Ensure proper focus states for all interactive elements
✅ Test with keyboard navigation
✅ Use system fonts for optimal performance
✅ Keep forms simple and clear

### Don'ts

❌ Don't use custom fonts without permission (use system fonts)
❌ Don't skip focus states or make them hard to see
❌ Don't use low contrast color combinations
❌ Don't create tiny touch targets (< 44px)
❌ Don't use decorative gradients or complex backgrounds
❌ Don't skip ARIA labels on form elements
❌ Don't use generic text like "Click here" for buttons

## Design Tokens Reference

All design tokens are defined in `frontend/src/index.css`:

```css
--color-primary: hsl(203 100% 35%);          /* Rijksblauw */
--color-primary-foreground: hsl(0 0% 100%);  /* White */
--color-destructive: hsl(0 84% 50%);         /* Red */
--color-border: hsl(220 15% 85%);            /* Light gray */
--color-input: hsl(220 15% 85%);             /* Light gray */
--color-ring: hsl(203 100% 35%);             /* Focus ring */
```

